From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] toolkit: pass the shell Activity ID to the GTK4 entrypoint

The shell allocates the instance ID and exports it in the child environment,
but activityinstance only reads its parser argument and otherwise generates a
second random ID. Pass the shell ID explicitly so the Activity D-Bus service,
Casilda client, and shell model refer to the same instance.

---
 src/sugar4/activity/activityfactory.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/sugar4/activity/activityfactory.py b/src/sugar4/activity/activityfactory.py
--- a/src/sugar4/activity/activityfactory.py
+++ b/src/sugar4/activity/activityfactory.py
@@ -118,7 +118,8 @@ def create(bundle, handle):
         _notify_launch_failed(handle.activity_id)
         return None
     command = [command[0], bundle.get_path(), *command[1:]]
+    command.extend(["--activity-id", handle.activity_id])
     environment = get_environment(bundle, handle)
